  "uid": "ss-pipeline",
  "title": "Session Sitter — the offline pipeline",
  "description": "The offline path: what `session-sitter learn` read, what it refused and why, and what it proposed. Reads kind:pipeline_run. A run that correctly produced nothing is a ROW here.",
  "templating": {
    "list": [
      {
        "name": "machine",
        "label": "machine",
        "type": "textbox",
        "query": ".*",
        "current": {
          "text": ".*",
          "value": ".*"
        },
        "options": [],
        "description": "A regexp over the machine field. `.*` is all of them; type a machine name to scope to one. A team-scope export carries a per-machine pseudonym here, so machines stay distinguishable from each other without being identifiable."
      }
    ]
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 19,
      "datasource": {
        "type": "victoriametrics-logs-datasource",
        "uid": "sessionsitter"
      },
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Read this first",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "### Why this reads run lines and not clause files\n\nA `learn` run that reads the trail, applies every gate and **correctly proposes nothing** writes no clause file and makes no commit. So a funnel built from surviving artefacts cannot tell that run apart from a scheduler that stopped firing three weeks ago — and those two have opposite meanings. One is the fail-closed design working exactly as designed; the other is an outage nobody has noticed.\n\n**A produced-nothing run is a success row, not a gap.** That is what the tile counts, and it is why `learn` writes a line per invocation whether or not it produced anything.\n\n`producedNothing` is true only for a `propose` run — an `accumulate` run folds new records and never proposes, so the outcome does not apply to it and the field says so rather than reading true on every one."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 20,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Did it run, and what happened",
